Subject: [PATCH 6/9] geph5-app: Android platform support in platform.rs

The single largest patch in the series, and the only one carrying real Android
behaviour rather than cfg widening. Four kinds of change:

  1. Real Android paths. state_dir() routes through manager_control's
     android_state_dir() (patch 0002): root installs resolve to
     /data/adb/geph5 — Android's root filesystem is read-only and has no
     /var/lib — while an unprivileged Termux install resolves to $HOME/.geph5.
     runtime_dir() follows the state dir, so runtime sockets stay under $HOME
     for Termux instead of the root-only /data/adb area.

  2. ensure_service_user() -> Ok(None). Android has no useradd/passwd
     management and the engine runs as root under KernelSU, so there is no
     service user to create or resolve.

  3. require_manager_privilege() returns Ok(()) on Android, split out of the
     linux/macos arm. One binary serves two install modes; proxy-mode
     operation — the only mode supported on Android — needs no privilege, so
     the manager may run unprivileged (the Termux install) and privilege is
     enforced lazily where it would actually matter.

  4. apply_kde() no longer errors without HOME. The boot environment has no
     HOME, and the KDE proxy path resolves per-user desktop config
     (kioslaverc) through $HOME. Requiring it made the manager fail to start on
     a headless root service. With no HOME there is by definition no desktop
     session, so skipping is correct, not a workaround. service.sh and
     termux-gephctl.sh also export HOME=/data/adb/geph5 at boot.

The remaining ~20 hunks are mechanical cfg widening (target_os = "linux" ->
any(linux, android)) across proxy application, privilege checks, shutdown
signal handling, engine spawning, systemd registration and path helpers.

Fragility: high, and it goes last for that reason. This file is 1946 lines and
upstream has touched it 8 times since 2025 (most recently 2026-08-24, in the
0.4.3 RNG refactor). If this patch rejects, do not hand-merge: re-derive it
with patches/regenerate.sh, because the cfg attributes move whenever upstream
moves the code they guard, and a manual fix-up can leave a tree that compiles
while targeting the wrong platform.

--- Linux side-by-side (added with the Nix build, 2026-11) ---
state_dir() and runtime_dir() also follow GEPH5_STATE_DIR on Linux, the
engine-side counterpart of the socket override in patch 0002: settings.json,
the cache, manager.log and the engine/engine.sock IPC socket all relocate
under the override, so a side-by-side install (shifted ports: SOCKS5/HTTP
via settings.json proxy.socks5_port/http_port, PAC via GEPH5_PAC_PORT from
patch 0008) never collides with /var/lib/geph or /run/geph of the official
install. Defaults are byte-identical with the variable unset.

Deliberately not segregated: the VPN-plane globals (nft table "geph",
TUN_IFACE, ip rules) — two installs are expected to run proxy mode only;
full-tunnel on both would fight over the kill switch regardless of paths.
